{# A declarative page with no report behind it.

   Server-rendered. A page is a manifest plus this template, so it needs no JavaScript to be a page:
   the filters are a plain GET form, the table is a table, and the totals are totals.

   A page that DOES name a report does not come through here — it renders through
   `reports/report.html.jinja` via `renderReportPage`, the same path `/reports/<key>` uses, because the
   manifest is the one page definition and the two routes are the same page.

   What this replaces: the shell used to embed the manifest as JSON and load
   `public/js/runtime/page.js`, which fetched `/p/<slug>/data` and built the table in the DOM. That
   was 171 lines of client JavaScript and an 8 MB response for a report `/reports` returns in 465 KB. #}
{% extends 'layout.html.jinja' %}
{% import 'partials/filters.html.jinja' as fl %}
{% import 'partials/table.html.jinja' as tb %}
{% block body %}
<h1 class="page-title">{{ meta.title }}</h1>

<form class="filters" method="get" action="">
{% for field in meta.fields %}{{ fl.render_field(field, filters, options) }}{% endfor %}
  <div class="filter-actions">
    <button class="btn primary" type="submit">APPLY</button>
    <a class="btn" href="">RESET</a>
    <button class="btn" type="button" data-print>PRINT</button>
  </div>
</form>

<div class="report" id="report">
{{ tb.simple(columns, rows, "cards") }}
{% include 'partials/totals.html.jinja' %}
</div>
{% endblock %}
